   "type": "line_radu",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_radu",
   "text": "Da, la zece fix. Chimie sau biologie — repet cu un coleg.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 650
  },
  {
   "id": "s008",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "Two new students on the first day. This time, the rules behind the verbs — the part the book leaves out — then six words.",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 1000
  },
  {
   "id": "s009",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "Romanian verbs come in groups, and you can tell the group from the dictionary form — the to-form. It ends in an a, an e-a, an e, an i, or an i with a hat. Each group has its own endings. Every verb in this lesson is in the first group, the a-group. Listen to three of them in their dictionary form:",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 800,
   "chapter": "The rule"
  },
  {
   "id": "s010",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_male",
   "text": "a asculta, a repeta, a explica",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 2200
  },
  {
   "id": "s011",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "To use one: take off the final a. That's the stem. Then add the ending for the person. For I: nothing. Listen:",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 400
  },
  {
   "id": "s012",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_female",
   "text": "eu ascult, eu repet, eu explic",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 2200
  },
  {
   "id": "s013",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "For you: an i. For he or she: the short uh. Listen:",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 400
  },
  {
   "id": "s014",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_male",
   "text": "tu asculți, el ascultă",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 2000
  },
  {
   "id": "s015",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "For we: uhm. For you all: ats. And they is exactly the same as he. Listen:",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 400
  },
  {
   "id": "s016",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_female",
   "text": "noi ascultăm, voi ascultați, ei ascultă",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 2400
  },
  {
   "id": "s017",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "So six persons, five endings: nothing, i, uh, uhm, ats, uh. Two small things change the sound. Before the i of you, a t becomes ts. Listen:",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 800
  },
  {
   "id": "s018",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_male",
   "text": "ascult, asculți; repet, repeți",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 2200
  },
  {
   "id": "s019",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "And some verbs shift their middle vowel too. That isn't a rule you can work out — learn it with the verb. Listen:",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 400
  },
  {
   "id": "s020",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
   "voice": "ro_female",
   "text": "învăț, înveți, învață; întreb, întreabă",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 2400
  },
  {
   "id": "s021",
   "type": "narration",
   "lang": "en",
   "voice": "en_narrator",
   "text": "One more thing for later. Many a-group verbs add an extra e-z before the ending — you used one yourself in the last episode. Listen:",
   "rate": 1.0,
   "pause_after_ms": 400
  },
  {
   "id": "s022",
   "type": "target",
   "lang": "ro",
